      "final_message": "Now I'll trace through the code:\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")`\n2. In `audit.py`, `write_audit(kind, ident, log=None)` is called with `kind=\"order\"` and `ident=\"7781\"`\n3. Line 11 has a redaction marker, but I need to determine what the actual key is\n4. Looking at the `_format_key` function on line 5-6, it formats as: `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`\n5. From `config.py`, `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"`\n6. So with `kind=\"order\"` and `ident=\"7781\"`: `f\"AUD-ORDER-7781\"` = `\"AUD-ORDER-7781\"`\n\nThe key that gets written to the audit log is the result of `_format_key(\"order\", \"7781\")`, which is `\"AUD-ORDER-7781\"`.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
